sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Admin as Administrator
    participant GrantTool as polar-admin-grant<br/>(admin's local tool)
    participant CertIssuer as cert-issuer

    Note over Admin,CertIssuer: One-time. A hard prerequisite for everything else --<br/>someone has to be first, with nothing else yet to vouch for them.

    Admin->>GrantTool: Run tool
    activate GrantTool
    GrantTool->>GrantTool: Generate keypair locally<br/>(private key never leaves this machine)
    GrantTool->>CertIssuer: Present kubectl-admin-backed<br/>Kubernetes credential + CSR<br/>(direct -- admins are not yet a<br/>Cassini participant at this point)
    activate CertIssuer
    CertIssuer->>CertIssuer: Validate the admin's Kubernetes<br/>credential (existing trust path,<br/>no new IdP config for admins)
    CertIssuer-->>GrantTool: Signed, ordinary Polar client cert<br/>(no more privileged than any agent's)
    deactivate CertIssuer
    GrantTool->>GrantTool: Store cert + key locally<br/>(reused for every future grant/revoke)
    deactivate GrantTool
